# 3D variant of input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic -- diff against that file for
# the full combustion/elastic setup and its conditioning notes; things that
# differ here: (1) amr.n_cell's z extent is set equal to the x extent so the
# mesh is isotropic (dx=dy=dz) over a full cubic domain instead of the base
# file's flattened 64-cell z slab; (2) the ignition heat_source IC is
# localized to a circular patch (radius = 1/8 of the domain's x length)
# centered on the domain's x-z axis, rather than spanning the entire x-z
# extent; (3) amr.n_cell is halved in all three directions (160^3, vs. an
# isotropic-mesh 320^3) to keep the 3D cell count tractable, with the packed-
# sphere psread eps/plane.eps below doubled (5um->10um, 20um->40um) to track
# the doubled dx (0.5mm/160 = 3.125um) and preserve the same interface
# smoothing width in grid cells; (4) the run segfaulted on the first time
# step at 160^3/0.5mm, so both geometry.prob_lo/hi and amr.n_cell are
# quartered again (domain 0.5mm->0.125mm, mesh 160->40) as a smaller
# debugging configuration -- this keeps dx fixed at 3.125um (so the psread
# eps values from (3) are still correct), and the heat_source ignition
# radius is quartered along with the domain so it stays 1/8 of the domain's
# x length. The pre-quarter full-size values are left in place as commented
# lines immediately below their active replacements, to restore the full
# run once the segfault is diagnosed.
#
#   mpirun -np 8 ./bin/lowmach-3d-clang++ input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_3d
#
# The XYZR file contains 659 AP spheres from a mechanically contracted Miller
# packing. The 3D case uses the spheres directly; the 2D case uses their z=0
# cross-section. AP occupies approximately 44% of the 3D bed volume and 49% of
# the 2D slice. AP and HTPB partial volume fractions are exact complements.
#
# WARNING -- elastic solver conditioning, and two defects worked around
# below purely from the input side (2026-08-02; see
# ~/.claude/plans/i-have-an-input-cached-phoenix.md for the full
# investigation -- code fixes were attempted and reverted, so everything
# here is an input-only mitigation, not a real fix):
#
# (1) AMR coarse/fine divergence (unconditional, code defect D2): with
# amr.max_level > 0, Operator<Grid::Node>::reflux() silently discards the
# coarse-side residual contribution at every coarse/fine boundary node. This
# was verified to make the elastic MLMG solve diverge with textbook linear
# residual growth (resid/bnorm climbing ~0.04-0.07/cycle, sustained over
# 1500 V-cycles) on this exact production case at every amr.max_level > 0
# tried (1 and 2), reproduced deterministically on STEP 1's very first
# solve, and independent of the modulus scaling in (2) below (identical
# growth curve at both the original and the rescaled moduli). There is no
# input-side fix for this -- it is a real bug in the AMR reflux code. The
# only way to avoid it without touching code is to eliminate AMR entirely:
# amr.max_level = 0 below, with amr.n_cell scaled up 4x (40x40x16 ->
# 160x160x64) to preserve the finest-level dx (~3.1um) the interface
# resolution relies on. This costs ~16x (2D) more cells everywhere, all the
# time -- there is no adaptive refinement left. eta/temperature/velocity
# _refinement_criterion and amr.regrid_int/grid_eff below are now inert
# (no-ops) as a result; left in place rather than deleted in case AMR is
# ever restorable here.
#
# (2) Force/stiffness mismatch (independent of AMR): elastic.void.model.*
# and the solid mu/kappa below were originally tuned in
# tests/LowMachElasticPressure's void-modulus sweep against that test's
# ~1 Pa forcing, then transplanted here where elastic.apply_fluid_pressure
# drives the solve with the real ~3 MPa chamber pressure -- a ~3e6x forcing
# increase with no corresponding stiffness increase. Confirmed directly:
# at the original moduli, STEP 1's "exact" Newton step (nriters=1) produced
# a full displacement norm of 3.5 CENTIMETERS against a 0.5mm domain (line
# search then clipped the accepted step to alpha=0.0039, still ~137um,
# comparable to the whole domain) -- badly violating the small-deformation
# regime NeoHookeanPredeformed's one-Newton-iteration solve assumes is
# exact. That oversized step corrupts the geometry the next elastic solve
# (10 steps later, resync_coeffs=1) resyncs coefficients from, and that
# solve then diverges catastrophically (resid/bnorm growing ~6 orders of
# magnitude per V-cycle, failing in 4 iterations) even at amr.max_level = 0
# where (1) cannot be the cause. Fix applied below: every mu/kappa (AP,
# HTPB, and the void model) scaled up by 1e4 uniformly, which preserves
# every solid/void contrast ratio (so the accuracy/stability sweep findings
# below still apply unchanged) while bringing the force/stiffness ratio
# back to a physically sane regime. Verified over 30 steps / 3 elastic
# solves (interval=10) at the scaled moduli: every solve now takes the full
# Newton step (alpha=1) with shrinking displacement norms (3.5um -> 0.44um
# -> 0.077um) as the interface settles, and MLMG converges to tol_rel=1e-8
# every time. NOTE: elastic displacement/stress is one-way (fluid->solid,
# see LowMach::UpdateModel) and does not feed back into the CFD/chemistry,
# so this rescaling has no effect on the reacting-flow physics -- only on
# whether the elastic diagnostic solve itself is numerically well-posed.
#
# Both of the above still ride on the pre-existing conditioning workarounds:
# MLMG coarsens right through the (few-cell-wide) diffuse solid/void
# interface, and coarse-level operators built from a large coefficient jump
# over 1-2 cells are garbage -- MLMG genuinely diverges, not just converges
# slowly (see tests/LowMachElasticPressure/Readme.rst, the
# 2d-pressure-1Pa-softvoid sub-case). elastic.max_coarsening_level below
# caps how far MG coarsens past the interface; this is what actually
# restores convergence, do not remove it without re-verifying convergence.
# Verified empirically here that raising it from 2 to 3 (one more MG level)
# still converges and roughly halves solve wall time (131s -> 57s per
# solve at this resolution); raising it further to uncapped (-1, 6 MG
# levels) reliably diverges within a handful of iterations. Do not push it
# past 3 without re-verifying.
#
# How soft to make the void (contrast ratios only -- the uniform 1e4 scale
# above does not change these): tests/LowMachElasticPressure's "Void
# modulus vs. solver stability and accuracy" sweep (Readme.rst) swept
# solid/void contrast from 1x to 1e5x, capped and uncapped. Findings that
# drove the void.model contrast below: (1) with the coarsening cap, MLMG
# stays stable with a flat ~12-18 iterations out to ~30,000x contrast, then
# costs more iterations near ~33,000x, and fails by 100,000x; (2) accuracy
# vs. contrast is NOT monotonic -- worst around contrast 3-30x (~1%),
# improving as contrast grows, and flattening to a ~0.3-0.5% discretization
# floor by ~1,000-3,000x, past which softer buys no more accuracy.
# void.model.mu/kappa below are chosen so every one of AP/HTPB's mu/kappa
# contrasts against the void lands in [~250x, ~2,100x]: inside the accuracy
# plateau (or its near-plateau approach), and with a >10x stability margin
# below the ~30,000x mark where the capped solver still ran flat.
#
# Tolerance-based solving (elastic.tol_rel/tol_abs, set explicitly below
# rather than left at default) is used instead of a fixed iteration count so
# a non-converged solve is visible rather than silently accepted.
# elastic.solver.max_iter below is raised from 1500 to 3000 -- with
# max_coarsening_level capped at 3 for conditioning reasons, convergence to
# tol_rel=1e-8 is slow (verified needing ~1650-2050 iterations across the 3
# solves tested), not divergent.

plot_file = output.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_3d
amr.plot_dt = 1.0e-4_s
amr.max_level = 0
# amr.n_cell = 160 160 160  # full-size mesh (0.5mm domain, dx=3.125um) -- see (4) above
amr.n_cell = 40 40 40
amr.max_grid_size = 20
amr.blocking_factor = 2
amr.regrid_int = 5
amr.grid_eff = 0.7
amr.nsubsteps = 1
amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition = 1
amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition_eta_min = 0.99
# Elastic fields (disp/stress/strain) are nodal; mirror them into the *cell*
# plotfiles too so they can be sampled the same way as the scalar fields.
amr.cell.all = 1
amr.node.any = 0

# Inert with amr.max_level = 0 above (see WARNING at top of file) -- left in
# place in case AMR is ever restorable here.
eta_refinement_criterion = 0.5
temperature_refinement_criterion = 1.0
velocity_refinement_criterion = 1.0

timestep = 1.0e-7_s
stop_time = 35_ms
dynamictimestep.on = 1
dynamictimestep.min = 1.0e-12
dynamictimestep.max = 5.0e-6
dynamictimestep.verbose = 0

integration.type = RungeKutta
integration.rk.type = 3

# geometry.prob_lo = -0.25_mm  -0.25_mm  -0.25_mm  # full-size domain -- see (4) above
# geometry.prob_hi =  0.25_mm   0.25_mm   0.25_mm
geometry.prob_lo = -0.0625_mm -0.0625_mm -0.0625_mm
geometry.prob_hi =  0.0625_mm  0.0625_mm  0.0625_mm
geometry.is_periodic = 0 0 0

# Gas species 0-5 retain the ordering required by the Rocfire mechanism:
# AP, binder, monopropellant, premixed, primary-flame, final-flame products.
system.amount = kmol
gas.mw = 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol
gas.thermo.type = rocfire
gas.thermo.rocfire.mw = 26.0_g/mol
gas.thermo.rocfire.cp_mass = 0.3_cal/g/K
gas.thermo.rocfire.Tref = 273.15_K
gas.transport.type = rocfire
gas.transport.rocfire.mw = 26.0_g/mol
gas.transport.rocfire.prandtl = 0.69
gas.transport.rocfire.lewis = 1.0
gas.transport.rocfire.lambda_a = 2.13037e-7_cal/cm/s/K^2
gas.transport.rocfire.lambda_b = 5.32743e-6_cal/cm/s/K
gas.eos.type = tpg

species.names = AP_gas HTPB_gas Mono Premixed Primary Final AP_solid HTPB_solid
AP_gas.mechanics = fluid
HTPB_gas.mechanics = fluid
Mono.mechanics = fluid
Premixed.mechanics = fluid
Primary.mechanics = fluid
Final.mechanics = fluid
AP_solid.mechanics = rigid_solid
HTPB_solid.mechanics = rigid_solid
AP_solid.reference_density = 1950.0_kg/m^3
HTPB_solid.reference_density = 920.0_kg/m^3
AP_solid.specific_heat = 1297.90_J/kg/K
AP_solid.thermal_conductivity = 0.4186_W/m/K
HTPB_solid.specific_heat = 2418.29_J/kg/K
HTPB_solid.thermal_conductivity = 0.1300_W/m/K

# Elastic constants, converted from representative literature isotropic
# (E, nu) values via mu = E/(2*(1+nu)), kappa = E/(3*(1-2*nu)):
#   AP crystal:    E ~ 21.6 GPa, nu ~ 0.14  -> mu ~ 9.47 GPa,  kappa ~ 10.0 GPa
#   HTPB binder:   E ~ 5.0 MPa,  nu ~ 0.499 (near-incompressible rubber)
#                                            -> mu ~ 1.67 MPa, kappa ~ 833 MPa
# These are representative orders of magnitude for the pure phases, not a fit
# to this specific formulation -- replace with measured/calibrated values if
# available. See the WARNING above regarding solver conditioning at these
# magnitudes.
AP_solid.elastic.model.mu    = 9.47e6 # true SI 9.47e9 -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
AP_solid.elastic.model.kappa = 1.00e8 # true SI 1.00e10 -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
HTPB_solid.elastic.model.mu    = 1.67e6 # = true SI value -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
HTPB_solid.elastic.model.kappa = 8.33e8 # = true SI value -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)

# Soft void: the gas region gets a small but nonzero modulus (in the same
# units as the solid moduli above, i.e. also 1e4x-rescaled -- see WARNING
# above) instead of being masked by psi's 1e-8 floor. This replaces the
# void's effective modulus of "full AP stiffness x 1e-8" with a true
# soft-material contrast and disables psi entirely (LowMach::Parse). Chosen
# per the tests/LowMachElasticPressure sweep so every solid modulus above
# sits ~250x-2,100x above these values: AP mu ~1,890x, AP kappa ~250x, HTPB
# mu ~330x, HTPB kappa ~2,080x -- inside/near the sweep's accuracy plateau
# and with >10x stability margin below where the capped solver was still
# verified stable (~30,000x). The 1e4x rescale above preserves these ratios
# exactly (both sides scaled together).
elastic.void.model.mu    = 5.0e3
elastic.void.model.kappa = 4.0e5

chemistry.model.type = rocfire
chemistry.model.rocfire.A = 27.0e3_g/cm^3/s 25.3e3_g/cm^3/s 5.0e3_g/cm^3/s 0.4e3_g/cm^3/s
chemistry.model.rocfire.pressure_exponent = 1.6 1.7 1.7 1.7
chemistry.model.rocfire.activation_energy = 15.9_kcal/mol 14.5_kcal/mol 11.3_kcal/mol 14.5_kcal/mol
chemistry.model.rocfire.qgas = 430.0_cal/g 447.0_cal/g 8365.0_cal/g 2127.0_cal/g
chemistry.model.rocfire.qsolid = -100.0_cal/g -300.0_cal/g
chemistry.model.rocfire.pressure_reference = 1.0_bar
chemistry.solver.type = backward_euler
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.max_iter = 100
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.reltol = 1.0e-8
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.abstol = 1.0e-12

# AP uses the 1-6 MPa monopropellant calibration from LMRFMonoAP. HTPB uses the
# approximately 4 mm/s calibration from the 3 MPa sandwich configuration.
# The phase-field gradient terms are integrated implicitly.
mechanisms.names = AP_decomposition HTPB_pyrolysis
AP_decomposition.type = phase_change
AP_decomposition.phase_change.in = AP_solid
AP_decomposition.phase_change.out = AP_gas
AP_decomposition.phase_change.rate_multiplier = 2.75e6
AP_decomposition.phase_change.activation_temperature = 3145.0_K
AP_decomposition.phase_change.temperature_cutoff = 360.0_K
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.type = allencahn
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.mobility = 0.01_1/Pa/s
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.lambda = 8.333333333333333_Pa
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.kappa = 1.0e-8_J/m
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w0 = 0.0
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w12 = 2.0
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w1 = 1.0

HTPB_pyrolysis.type = phase_change
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.in = HTPB_solid
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.out = HTPB_gas
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.rate_multiplier = 1.85e5
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.activation_temperature = 3145.0_K
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.temperature_cutoff = 360.0_K
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.type = allencahn
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.mobility = 0.01_1/Pa/s
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.lambda = 8.333333333333333_Pa
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.kappa = 1.0e-8_J/m
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w0 = 0.0
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w12 = 2.0
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w1 = 1.0

rigid.relaxation_time = 1.0e-8_s
rigid.velocity = 0.0 0.0 0.0

advection.type = muscl
advection.muscl.limiter.type = minmod
cfl = 0.8
phase_field.cfl = 1.5
include_viscosity = 1
implicit_viscosity = 1
include_conduction = 1
advect_temperature = 1
projection.enabled = 1
projection.tol_rel = 1.0e-11
projection.tol_abs = 1.0e-12
projection.verbose = 0
projection.update_pressure = 1
diffusion.tol_rel = 1.0e-11
diffusion.tol_abs = 1.0e-12
diffusion.verbose = 0
#diagnostics.interval = 100
diagnostics.extended_fields = 0

# The common diffuse condensed/gas surface is y=0. Both species read the same
# packing; inversion makes HTPB the exact complement of AP inside the bed.
AP_solid.density.ic.type = psread
AP_solid.density.ic.psread.file.name = input.lm.ap_htpb_packed.xyzr
AP_solid.density.ic.psread.file.unit = mm
AP_solid.density.ic.psread.slice.z = 0.0_mm
AP_solid.density.ic.psread.eps = 10.0_um
AP_solid.density.ic.psread.value = 1950.0_kg/m^3
AP_solid.density.ic.psread.plane.point = 0.0_mm 0.0_mm 0.0_mm
AP_solid.density.ic.psread.plane.normal = 0.0 -1.0 0.0
AP_solid.density.ic.psread.plane.eps = 40.0_um

HTPB_solid.density.ic.type = psread
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.file.name = input.lm.ap_htpb_packed.xyzr
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.file.unit = mm
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.slice.z = 0.0_mm
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.eps = 10.0_um
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.value = 920.0_kg/m^3
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.invert = 1
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.plane.point = 0.0_mm 0.0_mm 0.0_mm
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.plane.normal = 0.0 -1.0 0.0
HTPB_solid.density.ic.psread.plane.eps = 40.0_um

# The gas initially contains final products above the packed bed. Initialize
# the gas consistently with the thermal penetration profile so that pressure
# is uniform at startup.
#
# NOTE (2026-08-02): a "remove heat_source, start the fluid domain at 3000K"
# variant was tried and reliably crashes regardless of how the hot region is
# shaped (whole gas volume, or a thin layer at the interface): both pull the
# SOLID surface temperature up near its phase-change activation_temperature
# (3145K, see AP_decomposition/HTPB_pyrolysis below -- only ~150K above the
# 3000K flame temperature) at t=0, triggering a near-singular decomposition
# rate right at the interface that blows up the diffusion solve within a
# handful of steps, independent of the (already-fixed, see WARNING above)
# elastic solver. Reverted back to this file's original scheme -- matching
# input.lm.ap_htpb_packed, confirmed working there -- of a modest Tignite =
# 400K initial peak (safely below the 3145K activation temperature) plus a
# transient heat_source ramp that reaches ignition-sustaining temperatures
# gradually instead of instantaneously.
Final.density.ic.type = expression
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.P = 3.0e6
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.Tambient = 300.0_K
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.Tignite = 400.0_K
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.Lsolid = 100.0_um
Final.density.ic.expression.constant.Lgas = 250.0_um
Final.density.ic.expression.region0 = "max(0.0,(0.5+0.5*tanh(2.0*y/20.0e-6))*P/(319.787*(Tambient+(Tignite-Tambient)*exp(-max(-y,0.0)/Lsolid-max(y,0.0)/Lgas))))"

velocity.ic.type = constant
velocity.ic.constant.value = 0.0
temperature.ic.type = expression
temperature.ic.expression.constant.Tambient = 300.0_K
temperature.ic.expression.constant.Tignite = 400.0_K
temperature.ic.expression.constant.Lsolid = 100.0_um
temperature.ic.expression.constant.Lgas = 250.0_um
temperature.ic.expression.region0 = "Tambient+(Tignite-Tambient)*exp(-max(-y,0.0)/Lsolid-max(y,0.0)/Lgas)"
pressure.ic.type = constant
pressure.ic.constant.value = 3000000.0

# Apply the transient ignition flux used by the AP/HTPB sandwich case,
# localized to a circular patch (radius = 1/8 of the domain's x length)
# centered on the domain's x-z axis (x=0, z=0 -- the domain is centered on
# the origin, see geometry.prob_lo/hi above), rather than spanning the whole
# x-z extent as in the 2D/thin-slab base file. The radial cutoff is smoothed
# with the same tanh transition width used for the through-thickness (y)
# profile. radius is quartered along with geometry.prob_lo/hi above (see (4)
# at the top of the file) so it stays 1/8 of the domain's x length.
heat_source.ic.type = expression
heat_source.ic.expression.unit = W/m^3
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.qflux = 1.0e7_W/m^2
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.width = 6.25e-6_m
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.norm = 1.772453850905516
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.toff = 2.5e-4_s
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.tramp = 1.0e-5_s
# heat_source.ic.expression.constant.radius = 62.5e-6_m  # full-size domain's 1/8 x length -- see (4) above
heat_source.ic.expression.constant.radius = 15.625e-6_m
heat_source.ic.expression.region0 = "qflux*exp(-(y/width)^2)/(norm*width)*0.5*(1.0-tanh((t-toff)/tramp))*0.5*(1.0-tanh((sqrt(x^2+z^2)-radius)/width))"

component_density.bc.type = constant
component_density.bc.constant.type.xlo = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.xhi = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.ylo = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.yhi = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.zlo = neumann
component_density.bc.constant.type.zhi = neumann

velocity.bc.type = constant
# Slip walls: reflect the wall-normal component oddly and tangential
# components evenly. The z walls are the 3D analogues of the x walls.
velocity.bc.constant.type.xlo = REFLECT_ODD REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_EVEN
velocity.bc.constant.type.xhi = REFLECT_ODD REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_EVEN
velocity.bc.constant.type.ylo = dirichlet
velocity.bc.constant.type.yhi = neumann
velocity.bc.constant.type.zlo = REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_ODD
velocity.bc.constant.type.zhi = REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_EVEN REFLECT_ODD
velocity.bc.constant.val.ylo = 0.0

temperature.bc.type = constant
temperature.bc.constant.type.xlo = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.xhi = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.ylo = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.yhi = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.zlo = neumann
temperature.bc.constant.type.zhi = neumann

pressure.bc.type = constant
pressure.bc.constant.type.xlo = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.type.xhi = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.type.ylo = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.type.yhi = dirichlet
pressure.bc.constant.type.zlo = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.type.zhi = neumann
pressure.bc.constant.val.yhi = 3000000.0

# Elastic solve over the condensed (rigid_solid) phase, driven purely by the
# local gas pressure (elastic.traction = 0, elastic.apply_fluid_pressure = 1
# -- see LowMach::UpdateModel and tests/LowMachElasticPressure). The bed
# regresses (mechanisms.names above), so rigid_eta moves and the elastic
# solve must be re-run periodically to track it; elastic.interval throttles
# this against the ~1e-7-5e-6s advective/chemistry timestep so the 1-Newton-
# iteration MLMG solve (default elastic.nriters = 1, see
# Base::Mechanics::Register) does not dominate runtime.
elastic.type = static
elastic.interval = 1000
#elastic.dt = 1e-4_s
elastic.traction = 0.0
elastic.apply_fluid_pressure = 1
elastic.etacutoff = 0.0
#elastic.print_model = 1
elastic.solver.verbose = 4
# Tolerance-based (not elastic.solver.fixed_iter): a stalled/non-converged
# solve should be visible rather than silently accepted at these moduli --
# see the WARNING at the top of this file.
elastic.tol_rel = 1.0e-8
elastic.tol_abs = 1.0e-8
# Required alongside elastic.void.model.* below: MLMG coarsens right
# through the diffuse solid/void interface, and at this modulus contrast
# that produces garbage coarse-level operators (verified in
# tests/LowMachElasticPressure's 2d-pressure-1Pa-softvoid sub-case, which
# diverges outright without this cap). See the WARNING above -- raised from
# 2 to 3 (verified stable, ~2x faster); do not push further (uncapped
# diverges within a handful of iterations).
elastic.max_coarsening_level = 0
elastic.solver.conservative_face_flux = 1
elastic.solver.line_search = 1
elastic.solver.resync_coeffs = 1
# A single Newton iteration is exact for this problem regardless: from the
# zeroed initial guess set by elastic.zero_out_displacement (Base::Mechanics
# default), NeoHookeanPredeformed linearizes exactly about F = I (see
# tests/LowMachElasticPressure/Readme.rst's derivation), so nriters > 1 buys
# no accuracy here. It does cost stability: with nriters = 3 the accepted
# first-iteration step is tiny (line search alpha ~= 0.004, residual barely
# reduced), and the resync_coeffs rebuild for the 2nd Newton iteration then
# diverges catastrophically -- independent of the void modulus above (tried
# 0.1 and 10 with identical behavior) -- so this is a separate conditioning
# issue in the multi-Newton path at these moduli, not something the void
# model fixes. Confirmed nriters = 1 converges end-to-end (see the void
# modulus comment above); revisit only if this problem stops being an
# effectively-linear F=I configuration (e.g. nonzero initial displacement
# carried over between elastic.interval solves at large deformation).
elastic.solver.nriters = 1
elastic.solver.nrtolerance = 0
# Raised from 1500 -- see WARNING above (max_coarsening_level=3 caps MG
# effectiveness, so convergence to tol_rel is slow, not divergent; verified
# needing ~1650-2050 iterations).
elastic.solver.max_iter = 100000
elastic.solver.pre_smooth = 2
elastic.solver.post_smooth = 2
elastic.solver.bottom_solver = smoother
allow_unused=True

# BCs mirror the velocity slip-wall/open-top setup above, per component
# (x,y[,z]): x/z faces are rollers (normal displacement clamped, shear
# traction-free, matching REFLECT_ODD/REFLECT_EVEN); ylo (solid substrate) is
# fully clamped; yhi (open gas boundary) is fully traction-free. Edges and
# corners take the per-component intersection of their adjacent faces
# (displacement wins over traction where they conflict) -- see the
# consistency warning in BC/Operator/Elastic/Constant.H.
elastic.bc.type = constant
elastic.bc.constant.type.xlo = disp trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhi = disp trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.ylo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.yhi = trac trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.zlo = trac trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zhi = trac trac disp
# 3D edges / 2D corners
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloylo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiylo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloyhi = disp trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiyhi = disp trac trac
elastic.bc.constant.type.ylozlo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.ylozhi = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.yhizlo = trac trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.yhizhi = trac trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zloxlo = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zloxhi = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zhixlo = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.zhixhi = disp trac disp
# 3D corners
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloylozlo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloylozhi = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiylozlo = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiylozhi = disp disp disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloyhizlo = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xloyhizhi = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiyhizlo = disp trac disp
elastic.bc.constant.type.xhiyhizhi = disp trac disp
